  "decisions": [
    "Every actual exported form wrapper and private native Choice subpart has stable slot identity. Native 64px minimum answer card,10px corner,16px indicator/8px dot and 20px shortcut role remain semantic tokens; preferred 448px form width is capped by its parent and answers grow for longer text. Radio/checkbox decoration follows actual data-type/data-checked; invisible native input still owns focus, labels, selection and FormData. Focus-visible is projected on the actual containing label, not an invented role. Inactive Item and inapplicable action hidden/inert states remain hidden despite flex/grid layout; errors use actual registered alert/description semantics. Source-independent fixtures include required/optional, single/multiple, text/error and focus. Source active item, native answers, skip participation and submission validity are separate authorities. Source Ctrl/Meta+Enter and optional letter shortcuts remain real primitive behavior, never generic value transitions. Preferred spacing/type sizes and 44px form actions are explicit readable reference decisions. No page coordinates, source ID anatomy or hidden native answer replacement.",
    "Semantic token scalar values are meaningful reusable metrics, never coordinate-keyed specimen dimensions. Widths in native specimen grids remain evidence unless explicitly adopted as a domain layout constraint."
  ]
